@startuml
title Route boundaries and neighboring owners
left to right direction
rectangle "Network\nCurrent authenticated facts" as Network
rectangle "Admission\nFinite rights and irreversible spend" as Admission
rectangle "Hosting\nPhysical reservations" as Hosting
rectangle "Route\nSelection and protected transport" as Route
rectangle "Endpoint\nLive authority and scenario composition" as Endpoint
rectangle "Publication\nRegistration authority" as Publication
rectangle "Reachability\nVerified Descriptor and history" as Reachability
rectangle "Execution\nJob and Grant" as Execution
rectangle "Service Connection\nInstance authentication and continuity" as Connection
rectangle "Node\nDuty and process supervision" as Node
Network --> Route
Admission --> Route
Hosting --> Route
Endpoint --> Route
Publication --> Endpoint
Reachability --> Endpoint
Execution --> Endpoint
Route --> Connection
Endpoint --> Connection
Node --> Route
note bottom of Route
  Relationships describe evidence and operations,
  not permitted Go imports or an event bus.
  Route is not one cross-principal aggregate.
  Endpoint, Node and Service neighbors denote
  future new owners, not old runtime imports.
end note
@enduml
